Subject: Phase3 Topology Machine Forms Requirement Matrix

@ [canonical] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Phase3_Topology_Machine_Forms.sop

& [MatrixIdentity] is M2A implementation accounting
  + [matrix_uuid] is ddaf5b01-cc7a-4e34-9873-dc987f9e8368
  + [status] is complete

& [P3TF-001] is strict JSON and bounded faults
  + [proof_route] is unknown field, unknown enum, malformed JSON, and bounded diagnostic tests
& [P3TF-002] is hard positive scan limits
  + [proof_route] is zero, ceiling, file-total coherence, and valid boundary tests
& [P3TF-003] is canonical strong identity
  + [proof_route] is length, lowercase, hexadecimal, and round-trip tests
& [P3TF-004] is coherent entry and content evidence
  + [proof_route] is complete kind-mode-path-content table tests
& [P3TF-005] is sorted unique bounded stream evidence
  + [proof_route] is default, named, duplicate, ordering, and count tests
& [P3TF-006] is canonical root-versus-descendant path semantics
  + [proof_route] is root absence and traversal, separator, colon, .git, and bounds tests
& [P3TF-007] is complete receipt binding and honest consistency
  + [proof_route] is every digest, count, total, profile, and freshness field test
& [P3TF-008] is in-range immutable consumption evidence
  + [proof_route] is before-issued, at-issued, before-expiry, and at-expiry tests
& [P3TF-009] is honest runtime-fault consequence
  + [proof_route] is Boolean consequence and changed-during-scan tests
& [P3TF-010] is no effect surface plus global verification and rollback
  + [proof_route] is source/API scan, lint, debug, release overflow, docs, audit, evidence, proof, and rollback
